A1. If you're a bootlegger the wages of sin are paid in this. ~ CASH
A4. To give the raspberry (high hat). ~ ROAST
A9. Members of a tribe of American Indians recently discovered by crossword fans. ~ UTES
A12. Man's nickname. ~ ED
A13. These people lead a just life; they either just make their train or just miss it. ~ COMMUTERS
A16. Chemical symbol for the stuff in a Yankee jitney. ~ NI
A17. Kind of stockings (obsolete). ~ LISLE
A19. What the Egyptian pyramid builders probably did when the twelve o'clock whistle blew. ~ ATE
A20. All book agents. ~ PESTS
A22. The famous crossword fish. ~ EEL
A23. This follows when husbands come home at 3 A.M. ~ ROW
A24. Something that bobs don't need. ~ NET
A25. The result of trying to pay the rent in modern apartment houses. ~ RUIN
A29. What the boss doesn't say when you ask for a raise. ~ SURE
A30. Underworld mansions. ~ DUMPS
A33. His "royal nibs." ~ NABOB
A35. What monkeys hang by. (Two-word version.) ~ DETAIL
A36. What bargain sales result in. ~ ONRUSH
A38. The kin you love to touch. ~ PA
A39. Something we want in a bathtub. ~ PRIVACY
A40. By. ~ AT
A41. What barbers do to bobbed heads. ~ RECLIP
A44. A gap or break (new crossword teaser). ~ HIATUS
A48. People who sing in these should practice what they screech. ~ DUETS
A49. A Spanish mister. ~ SENOR
A51. What storms and wives do. ~ RAGE
A54. As black as the ace of spades. ~ EBON
A56. A woman's secret. ~ AGE
A58. What herds gently do as they wind over the lea. ~ LOW
A61. A high flyer. ~ ACE
A62. This is like a wife, the longer you leave it standing round the more of a kick you get. ~ CIDER
A64. What villains say. ~ AHA
A65. The creator of a well-known inferno. ~ DANTE
A67. Patron saint of the wets. ~ AL
A68. What a pretty girl is likely to get. ~ CONCEITED
A71. This is easy. ~ EZ
A72. This runs up a shirt sleeve. ~ SEAM
A73. These go up but never come down. ~ RENTS
A74. A flapper's favorite fruit. ~ DATE

D1. A stalk a day keeps anæmia away. ~ CELERY
D2. Money talks, but this is what it says (Fr.). ~ ADIEU
D3. This gives wings to salaries (abbr.). ~ HCL
D4. Abbreviation for something that roomers exist in. ~ RM
D5. Good trade name for tent manufacturer. ~ OMAR
D6. These take life easily. ~ AUTOS
D7. The end of a perfect chicken. ~ STEW
D8. Topographical engineer (or what have you?) ~ TE
D9. What relatives like to do to us. ~ USE
D10. Come in! (High hat). ~ ENTER
D11. The kind of a girl men don't take out. ~ SISTER
D14. Over (poetic). ~ OER
D15. This is a mechanical term for how many times a room swings around per minute to the inebriate (abbr.). ~ RPM
D18. What the fans yelled at Kelley. ~ SLIDE
D21. We get them from the snooty. ~ SNUBS
D26. A crossword puzzle fan. ~ NUT
D27. These come from the cellar still. ~ SPIRITS
D28. A connoisseur of chickens. ~ FANCIER
D29. French coin. ~ SOU
D31. A tree, whose product helps to make the all-American breakfast. ~ MAPLE
D32. These come from banana skins. ~ SLIPS
D33. Whose ship made biblical history? ~ NOAHS
D34. A hardy quadrennial biped. ~ BRYAN
D35. Organization of ladies who perpetuate the spirit of '76 in the supposedly spiritless days of '25 (init.). ~ DAR
D37. The satisfactory form of the verb "to have." ~ HAS
D42. What razors get when they're sharpened. (Ask the man who hones one.). ~ EDGED
D43. A lot of good English is wasted on this kind of a ball. ~ CUE
D45. What friend wife makes hubby do to the line. ~ TOE
D46. Pertaining to a city. ~ URBAN
D47. What happens when two Irishmen meet. ~ FRACAS
D50. Advance agent for a cold. ~ SNEEZE
D52. The kind of pedestrian who gets a run for his money. ~ AGILE
D53. A name that never appears on a K. K. K. membership list. ~ COHEN
D55. This has sixteen legs and sings. ~ OCTET
D57. Every golf club has one (abbr.). ~ PRO
D58. How fat ladies keep in shape. ~ LACE
D59. Something that few waiters can do. ~ WAIT
D60. Kind of poem you don't mind. ~ ODE
D63. 1st, 2nd and 6th letters of word meaning "to be economical." ~ ECM
D66. The thing you don't like to do when you figure your income tax. ~ ADD
D69. Night rider (abbr.). ~ NR
D70. A high non-commissioned officer of the army (abbr.). ~ TS


